@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix mf: <http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/DataAccess/tests/test-manifest#> .
@prefix n3t: <http://example.org/n3/test#> .
<> a mf:Manifest ; mf:entries ( <http://example.org/n3/triple-term-conforming> ) .
<http://example.org/n3/triple-term-conforming> a n3t:Parse ; mf:name "triple-term-conforming" ; mf:action [ n3t:sourceDocument <case.n3> ] ; mf:result "triple-term-conforming" ; mf:status n3t:proposed ; rdfs:comment """A quoted triple term '<< >>' appears as the object term of the enclosing triple; the expected artifact is N3 because quoted-triple spelling is a dialect surface beyond classic N-Triples.""" .
